+      "description_en": "In May 2023 Voice of America reports that the military has consolidated its grip on the mobile operators since the coup: all four providers, Mytel, ATOM, Ooredoo and MPT, are directly or indirectly linked to the military, making sensitive user data more easily accessible. Experts such as Freedom House researcher Kian Vesteinsson warn of risks to source safety and the safety of journalists; independent media workers are considered most at risk. According to experts, control over the mobile operators is part of the military's broader strategy to monitor and censor the internet."
